  "term": "ultrasonic communication",
  "definition": "Ultrasonic communication is the exchange of signals through very high-frequency vocal sounds, studied in animals such as mice by recording and analyzing ultrasonic vocalizations. In behavioral research, these calls can be grouped into different types to help examine communication patterns.",
